@startuml
' UC15.3 - Cập nhật cấu trúc chương trình
autonumber "<b>0.</b> "
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor white
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor white
skinparam BoundaryBackgroundColor white
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor black
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor black
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam MaxMessageSize 200

' AS-IS evidence; paths are relative to the workspace root.
' UC: docs/uml/docs/LearnUP_UseCase.docx, UC15.3 row.
' BR: docs/uml/docs/LearnUP_QuyTacNghiepVu.docx, BR-85/88/89/147/284/285 and sections 5.2/5.3.
' Both requested DOCX files are under docs/uml/docs, not directly under docs.
' Their metadata revisions are 1; an identified business-spec release is not matched to a snapshot.
' docs/source-of-truth is absent; docs/architecture/source-of-truth-migration-plan.md:184 supports ownership.
' UI: frontend/src/pages/instructor/course.builder.structure.edit.tsx:18 (CourseBuilderStructureEdit),
' :32 (Submitted/reorder guards), :50/:59 (title changes), :94/:101 (moves), :117 (handleSave).
' Route: frontend/src/router.tsx:457/:459/:477 (Instructor builder, structure/edit).
' API: frontend/src/services/course.service.ts:106 (updateCourseStructureAPI); :1 uses courseAxios.
' Transport: frontend/src/services/axios.customize.ts:47/:61/:64; frontend/src/config/env.ts:13.
' Local development URL: frontend/.env.development:10 = http://localhost:8080.
' No local override env file was found; process VITE_COURSE_BACKEND_URL is unset.
' Gateway: gateway/api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:2/:40-43.
' Trusted claims: gateway/api-gateway/src/main/java/com/learnup/gateway/filter/JwtAuthenticationFilter.java:133.
' Bootstrap: services/course-service/src/main.ts:40-43 (api prefix, URI v1).
' Controller: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.controller.ts:134 (updateStructure).
' Service: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.service.ts:728 (updateStructure).
' Repository: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/courses.repository.ts:521 (updateStructure).
' DTO: services/course-service/src/modules/courses/dto/update-course-structure.dto.ts:14/:25/:42.
' Models: services/course-service/prisma/schema.prisma:18/:31/:67/:84/:104.
' Prisma adapter: services/course-service/src/infrastructure/prisma/prisma.service.ts:10;
' services/course-service/.env:2 selects course_db; credentials are not included here.
' Supporting refresh: UI:168; frontend/src/components/layout/layout.instructor.course.tsx:35;
' frontend/src/services/course.service.ts:55; courses.controller.ts:73; courses.service.ts:195;
' courses.repository.ts:108 (backend files are under the courses module paths above).

actor Instructor
boundary "Edit Course Structure Page" as Screen
participant ":ApiGateway" as Gateway
participant ":CoursesController" as Controller
participant ":CoursesService" as Service
participant ":CoursesRepository" as Repository
database "course_db" as CourseDB

' Preconditions: authenticated Instructor, valid Course route ID and loaded builder context.
' Entry: /instructor/courses/{courseId}/builder/structure/edit.
' Parent-layout initial tree loading is UC15 preparation; the editor copies it from useOutletContext.
' JWT/internal-key middleware and token refresh are preconditions, not the main UC interaction.
' Diagram uses verified local development configuration; other build modes/live requests are unverified.

activate Instructor
Instructor -> Screen: Open Edit Course Structure
activate Screen
Screen -> Screen: Check Submitted state
activate Screen
deactivate Screen

alt Editing checked successfully
  ' Not Submitted: title inputs are editable even when Locked.
  ' Reorder buttons and move handlers are disabled when Locked; Lesson moves stay within their Module.
  Instructor -> Screen: Rename titles; reorder only if Unlocked
  Instructor -> Screen: Select Save Structure
  Screen -> Screen: Normalize and validate titles
  activate Screen
  deactivate Screen

  alt Titles validated successfully
    ' One request for title changes, reordering or both. No separate rename/reorder API exists here.
    ' Payload is the full existing tree: modules[{id,title,lessons[{id,title}]}]; array order is desired order.
    Screen -> Gateway: PUT /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/structure\nComplete ID/title tree in desired order
    activate Gateway
    Gateway -> Controller: PUT /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/structure\nTrusted user context
    activate Controller
    Controller -> Service: Update Course structure
    activate Service
    Service -> Service: Verify Instructor and organization
    activate Service
    deactivate Service
    ' Service trims titles and rejects empty titles; DTO validates nested UUIDs/strings/200-char limits.

    ' Outcome-level alternative: expand the successful transaction; rejected attempts are summarized.
    ' No successful write is implied after a failed business check in a failed operand.
    alt Structure updated successfully
      Service -> Repository: Save titles and requested order
      activate Repository
      ' One Prisma transaction, timeout 20000 ms, serializes updateStructure requests on the Course row.
      Repository -> CourseDB: Lock Course row FOR UPDATE\nCurrent organization
      activate CourseDB
      CourseDB -->> Repository: Course row locked
      ' The row-lock query checks Course ID/organizationId; ownership is checked by the next read.
      Repository -> CourseDB: Read current tree, status and lock state\nCurrent tenant and chain owner
      CourseDB -->> Repository: Owned Course structure
      Repository -> Repository: Check Submitted, IDs and Locked reorder
      activate Repository
      deactivate Repository
      ' Reject Submitted first. Then require the exact same unique Module IDs and each Module's Lesson IDs.
      ' No add/delete/ID replacement or moving a Lesson to another Module is accepted.
      ' Compare array order with persisted position order; Locked rejects any detected order change.

      opt Module or Lesson titles changed
        Repository -> CourseDB: Update changed Module and Lesson titles
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Titles updated
        ' Only different titles are written; title-only requests are valid while Locked.
      end
      opt Order changed while Unlocked
        Repository -> CourseDB: Reorder changed collections\nTemporary negatives, then positions 1..N
        CourseDB -->> Repository: Positions updated
        ' For changed Module order, move existing positions negative, then assign requested 1..N.
        ' Repeat those two passes per Module whose Lesson order changed; leave other collections alone.
        ' This avoids unique(courseId,position) / unique(moduleId,position) conflicts.
      end
      ' Commit all title/position changes together; failure rolls back the transaction.
      deactivate CourseDB
      Repository -->> Service: UPDATED; titleChanged and orderChanged
      deactivate Repository
      Service -->> Controller: updated=true and change flags
      deactivate Service
      Controller -->> Gateway: 200 OK\nUpdate result
      deactivate Controller
      Gateway -->> Screen: Structure update confirmed
      deactivate Gateway

      ' handleSave awaits refetchStructure before the success toast/navigation; retain this actual REST.
      ' Only its normal successful trace is expanded; independent refresh error behavior is noted below.
      Screen -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/structure
      activate Gateway
      Gateway -> Controller: GET /api/v1/courses/{courseId}/structure\nTrusted user context
      activate Controller
      Controller -> Service: Refresh Course structure
      activate Service
      ' getStructure rechecks Instructor/organization; findStructure again scopes the chain owner.
      Service -> Repository: Load owned Course structure
      activate Repository
      Repository -> CourseDB: Read ordered tree and Material flags\nCurrent tenant and chain owner
      activate CourseDB
      CourseDB -->> Repository: Course, Modules, Lessons and Material flags
      deactivate CourseDB
      Repository -->> Service: Refreshed tree
      deactivate Repository
      ' Lesson.required = materials.some(isRequired); Module.required = lessons.some(required).
      Service -->> Controller: Refreshed tree and derived states
      deactivate Service
      Controller -->> Gateway: 200 OK\nCourse structure
      deactivate Controller
      Gateway -->> Screen: Refreshed structure
      deactivate Gateway
      Screen -->> Instructor: Show "Course structure updated successfully."
      Screen -> Screen: Return to Course Builder
      activate Screen
      deactivate Screen
    else Structure policy check failed\nSubmitted or Locked reorder
      ' Restore incoming executions; actor/screen remain active through every alternative.
      activate Gateway
      activate Controller
      activate Service
      ' The same transaction locks/reads Course, then returns SUBMITTED or LOCKED without writes.
      ' Submitted rejects all updates. Locked rejects the whole payload if order changed,
      ' including any accompanying title changes; there is no partial title save.
      ' This branch covers stale UI state or a crafted request: normal UI disables these actions.
      Service -->> Controller: Structure change rejected (409)
      deactivate Service
      Controller -->> Gateway: 409 Conflict
      deactivate Controller
      Gateway -->> Screen: Update rejected
      deactivate Gateway
      Screen -->> Instructor: Show "Unable to save Course structure."
    else Structure access or payload check failed
      activate Gateway
      activate Controller
      activate Service
      ' Role/context -> 403 before Repository; invalid DTO/empty normalized title -> 400.
      ' Scoped Course missing/wrong tenant/wrong chain owner -> NOT_FOUND -> 404.
      ' Duplicate/missing/foreign IDs or different Lesson membership -> INVALID_STRUCTURE -> 409.
      ' Partial failed reads are summarized; technical DB failures roll back writes and produce an error.
      Service -->> Controller: Access, validation or persistence error
      deactivate Service
      Controller -->> Gateway: 400 / 403 / 404 / 409 / 500
      deactivate Controller
      Gateway -->> Screen: Update error
      deactivate Gateway
      Screen -->> Instructor: Show "Unable to save Course structure."
    end
  else Title validation failed
    ' Trimmed title must be nonempty and <=200 chars; no HTTP request is sent.
    Screen -->> Instructor: Show Module or Lesson title warning
  end
else Editing check failed\nCourse is Submitted
  ' The component displays this read-only warning instead of the editor; handleSave also exits early.
  Screen -->> Instructor: Show "Course is awaiting approval."
end
deactivate Screen
deactivate Instructor

' BR-85/89/285: Locked allows title-only changes; Locked reorder and Submitted updates are rejected.
' BR-284: Published+Unlocked can be reordered; there is no Draft/Rejected-only guard in this UC.
' The implemented status check specifically excludes Submitted; no extra status rule is invented.
' BR-88: adding/deleting components is outside this route and prevented by exact ID-set validation.
' BR-147: Module/Lesson have no stored isRequired. No required flag appears in the PUT payload.
' The supporting GET derives required from Material flags; no Material or Lesson content is modified.
' Titles and order can change together in the one PUT when allowed. Reorder uses sibling arrays only.
' A no-op or empty valid tree returns updated=true with false change flags; it creates no components.
' Course row locking serializes this updateStructure method; other mutation paths were not proven
' to share this locking protocol. The client sends no revision token; unchanged membership alone
' does not detect concurrent title edits, so a later stale payload can overwrite an earlier edit.
' UI failures: the HTTP interceptor resolves server error envelopes without data.updated;
' handleSave throws its fixed Error, usually hiding the server-specific 409/404 reason.
' On PUT success, refetchStructure catches its own GET errors, clears structure and resolves.
' The editor may therefore show the success toast and navigate while the parent shows a load error.
' A refresh failure does not undo committed changes; no extra refresh-failure branch is expanded.
' UI changes its local arrays only until Save; changing a title or pressing an arrow makes no request.
' Parent-layout Assignment reads on route changes belong to shared outline preparation and are omitted.
' TenantClient/LearningClient/storage are injected but updateStructure/getStructure do not call them.
' No cross-service REST, storage provider, presigned URL, Kafka, outbox event or shared database access.
' Initial UC15 tree browsing, component creation/deletion and UC16.1 Lesson content editing are excluded.
@enduml
